`--config-file` reads the tracker block straight from a file, which is what lets a caller
outside any vault — no .booping marker anywhere above the cwd — run the tracker at all.

-- fixtures/cwd/tracker.yaml --
driver: cli
-- cmd --
booping-tracker --config-file tracker.yaml states --team ENG
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
states ENG: cli driver, no-op
-- stderr --
